    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **260 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format from `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 now builds the code from three parts:\n- **CITY3**: upper-cased first three letters of the owner's city\n- **LAST3**: upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- **NNNN**: a *per-city* 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of owners already in that city (matched case-insensitively, excluding the owner itself), replacing the previous global `findAll().size()` count.\n\nThe city is available at this step because `BuildOwner` (which runs earlier via `ApplyOwner`'s mapping) sets it on the entity before `AssignCustomerCode`.\n\n**Derived values rebuilt:** the only value derived from `customerCode` is `membershipNumber` (`AssignMembershipNumber`), which reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly and therefore automatically picks up the new format (`<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>-M<YY>`, e.g. `SYD-SMI-0007-M26`). I updated its javadoc example to match; no logic change was needed there.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserting `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) passes, along with all pre-existing tests.",
